note The fields split two ways. The reader's part survives frames: reveals opened, auto_open (the off-path root whose callers and callees were opened for it, so closing them afterwards sticks), root (that off-path root, kept as a root of the tree while the reader moves around inside the graph), collapsed (nodes cut to a preview), context (lines widened above and below), manual (dragged positions in fractional cells, which override the layout for as long as the node exists), the drag in progress, pan (pixels) and zoom, direction (left to right or top to bottom), the camera wishes look and fit with keep, the node a button asked to hold still, steering (who inside the graph is about to change the focus), glide (a pan in flight), keyboard (whether the last press was inside the canvas, which gives the arrows to the graph) and presence (whether the graph was on screen last frame). The frame's part is replaced every frame: built (this frame's Built), hits (hit rectangles in window pixels, read by the next frame's input), code_top (the pixel y of each node's first code row) and cell (the frame's cell size in pixels).

